## ╔══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╗
## ║        MASTER CONTEXT — READ BEFORE ALL PROMPTS         ║
## ╚══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╝

You are building **StudyOS** — an enterprise-grade, AI-powered study platform
for Indian competitive exam students (NEET 2026, JEE). Think: Notion + NotebookLM
+ personalized AI tutor + progress tracker — built specifically for Indian students.

STACK (non-negotiable — see docs/architecture/FINAL_ARCHITECTURE.md for authority):
  Frontend:  Next.js 15 (App Router) + React 19 + TypeScript strict + Tailwind CSS + shadcn/ui
  State:     TanStack Query v5 (server state) + Zustand (global UI) + Dexie.js (offline IndexedDB)
  Backend:   Supabase (PostgreSQL + Auth + Storage + Edge Functions + Realtime)
  AI:        LangGraph agents + multi-provider LLM router (user's own API key OR shared)
  Vector:    pgvector (Supabase extension) for NCERT RAG
  Cache:     Upstash Redis (rate limiting + session cache)
  Analytics: PostHog (self-hosted or cloud) + Tinybird for ClickHouse
  Payments:  Razorpay (India) + Stripe (international)
  Notifs:    Supabase Realtime + FCM (push) + WhatsApp Business API
  Deploy:    Vercel (frontend) + Supabase (backend)
  Monitoring: Sentry + LangSmith (AI tracing) + Uptime Robot

CORE PRINCIPLES:
  1. Student data (API keys, notes, progress) stays on device when possible
  2. Mobile-first (80% of Indian students use Android phones)
  3. Works offline for core features (checklist, notes, roadmap view)
  4. Multi-language: English + Tamil + Hindi + Telugu (at least English first)
  5. Accessibility: WCAG 2.1 AA minimum
  6. Performance: LCP < 2.5s, FID < 100ms, CLS < 0.1

ALWAYS in generated code:
  ✅ TypeScript strict mode
  ✅ Loading + error + empty states for every async operation
  ✅ Optimistic UI updates with rollback on failure
  ✅ Mobile-responsive Tailwind classes (sm: md: lg: breakpoints)
  ✅ JSDoc comments on all exported functions/components
  ✅ Zod validation on all API inputs/outputs
  ✅ Row Level Security on all Supabase tables
  ✅ Error boundary wrappers on all major UI sections

NEVER:
  ❌ Hardcode API keys anywhere
  ❌ Store LLM provider keys in database (localStorage/IndexedDB ONLY)
  ❌ Render user-generated content without DOMPurify sanitization
  ❌ Skip loading states ("it just flashes")
  ❌ Use any → use proper TypeScript types

