## ╔══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╗
## ║  PROMPT 1 — ENTERPRISE DATABASE SCHEMA (SUPABASE)       ║
## ╚══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╝

Generate the complete enterprise Supabase PostgreSQL schema for StudyOS.

REQUIREMENTS:

Part A — SQL Migration Files (numbered: 001_, 002_, etc.)

001_auth_and_users.sql:
  - users table extending Supabase auth.users
  - institutes table (multi-tenant: coaching centers can white-label the app)
  - institute_members (users ↔ institutes with roles: student/teacher/admin)
  - batches (teacher's class groups)
  - user_devices (for push notification tokens per device)
  - RLS: users see only own row; teachers see students in their batch; admins see institute

002_syllabus.sql:
  - exam_profiles (NEET2026, JEE_MAINS_2026, etc. — versioned)
  - subjects (Physics/Chemistry/Biology per exam)
  - chapters (with tier 1/2/3, weightage_pct, is_deleted, ncert_ref, class 11/12)
  - topics (under chapters, is_high_yield flag)
  - subtopics (with definition, is_high_yield, is_deleted, difficulty enum)
  - RLS: public read (no auth required for syllabus browsing)

003_progress.sql:
  - user_chapter_progress (completion %, confidence 1-5, revision_count)
  - subtopic_completions (idempotent: unique user_id+subtopic_id; timestamps)
  - study_sessions (start/end, chapters studied, total_minutes)
  - streaks (current, longest, last_study_date, freeze_used bool)
  - RLS: own rows only + teachers read student rows in batch

004_notes.sql:
  - notes (content_md, source_type enum, file_url, extracted_topics jsonb)
  - note_versions (full history)
  - note_embeddings (chunk_text, embedding vector(1536), chunk_index)
  - RLS: own notes only; institute notes visible to institute members

005_roadmap.sql:
  - roadmaps (ai_reasoning, readiness_score 0-100, urgency_level enum)
  - week_plans (focus_theme, week_tip, daily_breakdown jsonb)
  - week_plan_chapters (action enum: new_study/revision/practice/mock)
  - RLS: own roadmaps only

006_quiz_and_questions.sql:
  - questions (source enum: PYQ/AI, year nullable, options jsonb, difficulty enum)
  - quiz_sessions (score, total_questions, time_taken_seconds)
  - quiz_responses (selected_option, is_correct, time_taken_seconds)
  - user_question_flags (saved/skipped/flagged per question per user)
  - RLS: own sessions; questions are public read

007_chat.sql:
  - chat_sessions (llm_provider, model_used, total_tokens, chapter_id FK nullable)
  - messages (role enum: user/assistant/system, content, tokens_used)
  - RLS: own sessions only

008_analytics.sql:
  - events (event_type, properties jsonb, session_id, device_type, app_version)
  - daily_stats (materialized: study_minutes, subtopics_completed, quiz_score_avg)
  - RLS: own events; admins read all institute events

009_payments.sql:
  - plans (name, price_monthly_inr, price_yearly_inr, features jsonb)
  - subscriptions (user_id, plan_id, status enum, period_start, period_end, razorpay_sub_id)
  - invoices (amount_inr, paid_at, receipt_url)
  - RLS: own subscription data

Part B — Supabase TypeScript Types
  - Full Database interface for all tables
  - Row, Insert, Update types for each table
  - Enum types matching PostgreSQL enums

Part C — Indexes (performance-critical)
  - chapter progress queries (user_id + chapter_id)
  - subtopic completion lookups (user_id + subtopic_id)
  - Note search (user_id + created_at, full-text index on content_md)
  - Vector similarity (ivfflat index on embeddings, lists=100)
  - Analytics time-series (user_id + created_at on events)

Part D — Database Functions
  - get_chapter_completion_pct(user_id, chapter_id) → float
  - get_subject_completion_pct(user_id, subject_id) → float
  - get_overall_readiness(user_id) → float
  - calculate_streak(user_id) → int
  - get_weak_chapters(user_id, limit=5) → table

Part E — Realtime subscriptions
  - Which tables need Realtime enabled and why
  - Subscription patterns for frontend (progress updates, notifications)

