## ║  PROMPT 3 — DESIGN SYSTEM + SKILL_DESIGN.md             ║
## ╚══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╝

Create the complete StudyOS design system AND generate SKILL_DESIGN.md.

Part A — Design Tokens (tailwind.config.ts):
  Colors:
    brand: indigo scale (50→950)
    physics: blue scale
    chemistry: violet scale
    biology: emerald scale
    tier1: red-500 (urgent/high priority)
    tier2: amber-500 (medium)
    tier3: gray-400 (low priority)
    success, warning, danger, info semantic tokens
    All tokens with dark mode variants

  Typography:
    fontFamily: Inter (latin), Noto Sans Tamil, Noto Sans Devanagari
    fontSize scale: xs(12) sm(14) base(16) lg(18) xl(20) 2xl(24) 3xl(32) 4xl(40) 5xl(48)
    fontWeight: normal(400) medium(500) semibold(600) bold(700)
    lineHeight: tight(1.25) snug(1.375) normal(1.5) relaxed(1.625) loose(1.75)

  Spacing: 4px grid: 1(4) 2(8) 3(12) 4(16) 5(20) 6(24) 8(32) 10(40) 12(48) 16(64)px
  Radius: none(0) sm(4) md(8) lg(12) xl(16) 2xl(24) full(9999)
  Shadow: elevation system (sm, md, lg, xl, 2xl) with dark mode variants
  Animation: duration-150 (micro) duration-300 (standard) duration-500 (emphasis)

Part B — Component Library (using shadcn/ui base + custom):
  Atoms (generate all with TypeScript props):
    Button: variant(primary/secondary/ghost/destructive/outline) + size(sm/md/lg/icon) + loading state + icon slot
    Input: with label, error, helper text, left/right adornment
    Checkbox: with label, indeterminate state, high-yield star variant
    Badge: subject-colored, tier-colored, status variants
    ProgressBar: animated fill, label, color by subject
    ProgressRing: SVG animated circle, center label, subject color
    Avatar: initials fallback, status dot, size variants
    Skeleton: text, card, avatar, ring variants
    Spinner: size variants, overlay variant

  Molecules:
    ChapterCard: progress ring, tier badge, weightage, chapter name, last studied
    SubtopicItem: checkbox, name, definition (expandable), badges (high-yield, deleted, difficulty)
    AIMessageBubble: user/assistant/system with markdown rendering, timestamp, copy button
    NoteCard: title, excerpt, subject tag, date, source type icon
    StatCard: metric + label + trend (up/down/neutral) + sparkline
    WeekPlanCard: week number, theme, chapter pills, daily breakdown accordion
    QuizCard: question, 4 options (A/B/C/D), reveal answer state, explanation

  Organisms:
    AppShell: responsive layout (bottom nav mobile, sidebar desktop)
    ChapterChecklist: full accordion with virtual scrolling for 50+ subtopics
    RoadmapCalendar: horizontal scrolling weeks with snap
    LLMChatPanel: floating/drawer/fullscreen modes, keyboard-aware on mobile
    AnalyticsDashboard: grid of StatCards + heatmap calendar + charts

Part C — Motion Design:
  Page transitions: slide-in-right (forward) / slide-in-left (back)
  Component enter: fade-in-up (150ms, ease-out)
  Component exit: fade-out (100ms, ease-in)
  Progress fill: left-to-right ease-in-out (300ms)
  Ring: clockwise ease-in-out (300ms)
  Confetti: burst on chapter complete milestone
  Streak pulse: fire emoji pulse animation

Part D — SKILL_DESIGN.md content:
  Generate a complete SKILL.md file that an AI coding assistant reads before
  generating any UI code for StudyOS. Include:
  - Design token reference table (color names → hex values)
  - Component usage guidelines with DO/DON'T examples
  - Responsive design rules (mobile-first breakpoints)
  - Accessibility requirements per component type
  - Dark mode implementation patterns
  - Animation dos and don'ts (performance-safe animations only)
  - Subject color usage rules (when to use Physics blue vs generic)
  - Tier badge usage rules
  - Empty state illustration guidelines
  - Loading state hierarchy (skeleton > spinner > text)

Output:
  - tailwind.config.ts (complete with all tokens)
  - globals.css (CSS custom properties for theming)
  - All component files in src/components/ui/ and src/components/app/
  - SKILL_DESIGN.md

