## ╔══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╗
## ║  PROMPT 4 — AI AGENT SYSTEM (LANGGRAPH + 21ST.DEV)      ║
## ╚══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╝

Build the complete AI agent system for StudyOS using LangGraph.
Use 21st.dev agent templates as the base where applicable.

SKILL_AGENTS.md (generate this file first):
  - Agent architecture overview
  - Tool naming conventions
  - State type definitions
  - Zod schema library for all agent outputs
  - Prompt template library (one per agent)
  - Guardrail patterns
  - Testing patterns for agents

Agent 1 — Tutor Agent (most critical):
  Base: 21st.dev ReAct Agent template
  Purpose: Answer NEET concept questions with NCERT-grounded responses
  LangGraph nodes:
    - classify_intent (is this a question, explanation request, or example request?)
    - retrieve_ncert (pgvector similarity search on NCERT corpus)
    - retrieve_student_notes (pgvector search on student's own notes for this chapter)
    - generate_answer (LLM call with retrieved context)
    - add_citations (inject NCERT chapter+page references)
    - check_scope (is this within NEET syllabus? reject if not)
  Tools:
    - ncert_search(query: string, chapter_id?: string, top_k: number): NcertChunk[]
    - student_notes_search(query: string, user_id: string, chapter_id: string): Note[]
    - pyq_search(topic: string, year?: number): Question[]
  System prompt template (include full prompt):
    - NEET-scoped, NCERT-grounded, cite chapter+page, use student's name
    - XML sandwich for student notes (prevent injection)
    - "If you don't know, say so — never guess in NEET"
  Output schema (Zod):
    { answer: string, citations: Citation[], confidence: 0-1, related_subtopics: string[] }

Agent 2 — Roadmap Agent:
  Base: 21st.dev Planning Agent template
  Purpose: Generate weekly study plan JSON
  LangGraph nodes:
    - load_student_context (profile + progress + exam date)
    - calculate_weeks_remaining
    - prioritize_chapters (tier 1 first if < 8 weeks; balanced if > 12 weeks)
    - build_weekly_schedule (fit chapters into available study hours)
    - generate_week_themes (creative theme names: "Genetics Marathon", "Electricity Week")
    - validate_schedule (ensure no overloading, Biology gets 50% time)
  Full system prompt + user prompt templates
  Output schema (Zod): full WeeklyRoadmap type

Agent 3 — Note Extraction Agent:
  Purpose: Extract topics from OCR'd student notes → map to NEET syllabus
  Input: raw OCR text (may be messy/noisy)
  LangGraph nodes:
    - clean_ocr_text (fix common OCR errors: rn→m, l→1, etc.)
    - extract_topics (identify chapter names, formulas, diagrams mentioned)
    - fuzzy_map_to_syllabus (match extracted topics to official chapter list, >75% similarity)
    - detect_gaps (subtopics in official chapter NOT mentioned in notes)
    - score_quality (how complete are these notes?)
  Output schema (Zod): ExtractionResult with topics, gaps, quality_score, suggestions

Agent 4 — Quiz Generator Agent:
  Purpose: Generate NEET-style MCQs for any chapter
  LangGraph nodes:
    - fetch_chapter_content (NCERT RAG for chapter)
    - fetch_pyq_examples (similar PYQs for style reference)
    - generate_stem (question text — precise, unambiguous)
    - generate_distractors (3 wrong options — plausible, not obviously wrong)
    - generate_explanation (why correct answer is right + why distractors are wrong)
    - validate_question (does it match NEET format? is it answerable in 90s?)
  Output schema (Zod): Question[]

Agent 5 — Weak Area Detector:
  Purpose: Analyze student behavior to identify weak areas
  Input: last 30 days of quiz_responses + study_sessions + subtopic_completions
  Analysis dimensions:
    - Quiz accuracy per chapter (< 60% = weak)
    - Time to complete subtopics (slow = struggling)
    - Revision frequency (not revised in 7+ days = forgetting)
    - AI question patterns (student keeps asking about same topic = confused)
  Output: WeakAreaReport { weak_chapters: Chapter[], recommendations: Action[], spaced_reps: SubtopicSchedule[] }

Agent 6 — Daily Motivation Agent:
  Purpose: Personalized morning message + today's study recommendation
  Input: student name, streak, today's roadmap, weak areas, exam days remaining
  Output: { greeting: string, tip: string, today_focus: Chapter[], motivational_score: 1-10 }
  Tone: friendly, encouraging, never preachy, culturally aware (Indian student context)

LLM Router (llm-router.ts):
  Unified LLMClient interface:
    call(params: {messages, model, temperature, max_tokens, stream?}): Promise<LLMResponse>
  Provider implementations:
    - OpenAI (gpt-4o, gpt-4o-mini, o3-mini)
    - Anthropic (claude-sonnet-4-6, claude-haiku-4-5)
    - Google (gemini-2.0-flash, gemini-2.5-pro)
    - Groq (llama-3.3-70b — fastest for simple tasks)
    - Ollama (localhost:11434 — offline/private option)
  Routing logic:
    - Simple Q&A → Groq llama (fastest, cheapest)
    - Complex reasoning (roadmap, strategy) → Claude Sonnet or GPT-4o
    - Vision/OCR assistance → GPT-4o or Gemini Flash
    - Offline → Ollama fallback
  Retry + fallback:
    - Primary fails 2x → switch to fallback provider
    - All cloud fails → Ollama if available → show helpful error
  Cost tracking:
    - Token counting (tiktoken for OpenAI, estimate for others)
    - Cost per session (shown to students using own API key)

Output:
  - src/agents/ directory with all 6 agents
  - src/lib/llm-router.ts
  - src/lib/rag-client.ts (pgvector search)
  - SKILL_AI_AGENTS.md
  - All Zod schemas in src/types/agents.ts

