## ║  PROMPT 5 — ENTERPRISE ANALYTICS SYSTEM                 ║
## ╚══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╝

Build the complete analytics system for StudyOS.

SKILL_ANALYTICS.md (generate first):
  - Event naming convention: snake_case, past tense verb (subtopic_completed)
  - Required properties on every event: user_id, session_id, timestamp, app_version, device_type
  - Event categories and their properties
  - Privacy rules: no PII in event properties (use user_id, not email)
  - How to add new events (checklist)

Part A — Event Tracking Library (src/lib/analytics.ts):
  track(event: EventName, properties?: EventProperties): void
  identify(userId: string, traits: UserTraits): void
  page(pageName: string, properties?: PageProperties): void
  reset(): void // on logout
  
  Event catalog (generate TypeScript union type for all events):
    // Onboarding
    onboarding_started, exam_profile_selected, exam_date_set, chapters_assessed, onboarding_completed
    // Study
    chapter_opened, topic_expanded, subtopic_completed, subtopic_uncompleted, chapter_completed
    study_session_started, study_session_ended, streak_achieved, streak_broken
    // AI
    chat_opened, message_sent, ai_response_received, chat_exported, suggestion_clicked
    // Notes
    note_upload_started, note_ocr_completed, note_extraction_completed, note_saved, note_deleted
    // Quiz
    quiz_started, question_answered, quiz_completed, quiz_score_achieved
    // Roadmap
    roadmap_generated, roadmap_viewed, roadmap_exported, week_plan_expanded
    // Auth
    user_signed_up, user_signed_in, user_signed_out, password_reset_requested
    // Engagement
    app_opened, app_backgrounded, feature_discovered, settings_changed
    // Payments
    upgrade_clicked, plan_selected, payment_completed, subscription_cancelled

Part B — PostHog Integration:
  - PostHog React provider setup
  - Feature flags (for A/B testing new features)
  - Session recording (with privacy masking on note content)
  - Heatmaps (understand where students tap)
  - Funnels: Signup → Onboarding → First study session → Streak day 7
  - Cohort analysis: students who use AI chat vs those who don't

Part C — Student Analytics Dashboard (UI):
  <AnalyticsDashboard /> with these sections:
  
  Overview Cards:
    - Total study time this week (hours + vs last week %)
    - Subtopics completed this week
    - Current streak (fire emoji + days)
    - NEET readiness score (0-100, with trend arrow)
    - Days until exam (countdown)
    - Predicted score range (e.g., "580–620 based on current pace")
  
  Study Heatmap:
    - GitHub-contribution-style calendar (last 52 weeks)
    - Color intensity = study minutes
    - Tooltip: "May 12 — 3h 20min studied, 14 subtopics completed"
  
  Chapter Completion Chart:
    - Horizontal stacked bar per subject (completed / in-progress / not started)
    - Click to jump to that chapter
  
  Velocity Chart:
    - Line chart: chapters completed per week (last 8 weeks)
    - Trend line showing if student is accelerating or slowing down
  
  Subject Balance Donut:
    - Time allocation: Physics X% / Chemistry Y% / Biology Z%
    - Recommendation if imbalanced (Biology should be ~50%)
  
  Weak Areas Table:
    - Top 5 weak chapters (by quiz score + recency)
    - Last quiz score, last reviewed date, action button ("Revise now")
  
  Weekly Report (auto-generated every Monday):
    - PDF-exportable summary
    - Shareable via WhatsApp (image format)

Part D — Institute Analytics (Teacher/Admin):
  - Class-wide chapter completion heatmap (chapters × students matrix)
  - Per-student progress table (sortable, filterable)
  - At-risk students alert (< 30% completion with exam < 12 weeks)
  - Quiz performance comparison (anonymous rank in class)

Part E — Business Analytics (Internal — Metabase dashboards):
  SQL queries for:
    - DAU/WAU/MAU by exam type and state
    - Feature adoption (% of users who used AI/notes/roadmap this week)
    - Conversion funnel (free → paid) with drop-off analysis
    - Institute growth (new signups, seat activation rate)
    - AI cost per DAU (token usage / active users)
    - Retention cohorts (D1, D7, D30, D90)

Output:
  - src/lib/analytics.ts (full implementation)
  - src/types/events.ts (all event types)
  - src/components/analytics/ (all dashboard components)
