## ║  PROMPT 7 — CORE STUDENT FEATURES (UI + LOGIC)          ║
## ╚══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╝

Build the 5 core student-facing features. Each must be production-grade.

Feature 1 — Chapter Checklist (most critical screen):
  <ChapterChecklist chapter_id /> with:
    - Virtual scrolling (react-virtual) for chapters with 50+ subtopics
    - Optimistic checkbox updates (update UI instantly, sync DB async)
    - Long-press on topic: "Mark all complete / incomplete"
    - Swipe left on subtopic: undo last completion
    - Chapter complete celebration (confetti + haptic on mobile)
    - Progress ring (animated SVG, updates in real-time)
    - "Ask AI" FAB (opens LLM chat with chapter context pre-loaded)
    - Keyboard navigation (Tab + Space for accessibility)
    Hooks: useChapterProgress(), useSubtopicCompletion(), useChapterChat()
    Performance target: 50 subtopics render in < 200ms; checkbox response < 50ms

Feature 2 — Note Upload + AI Extraction:
  <NoteUploadFlow /> multi-step:
    Step 1: File drop zone (drag-drop desktop; camera/gallery mobile)
      - Accept: JPEG, PNG, WEBP, PDF, TXT (validate MIME by magic bytes)
      - Preview before processing
    Step 2: OCR Processing (Tesseract.js in Web Worker — non-blocking)
      - Progress: "Reading page 1 of 3..."
      - Quality warning if image too blurry (Laplacian variance check)
    Step 3: AI Extraction (send OCR text to Note Extraction Agent)
      - Streaming response (show topics appearing one by one)
      - "75% confident this is about: Genetics, Chapter 23"
    Step 4: Review + Confirm
      - Extracted topics as cards (accept/reject/remap each)
      - Syllabus gap warning: "Your notes don't mention: crossing over, chiasma"
      - "Add to my notes" → saves with chapter tags
    Hooks: useNoteUpload(), useOCR(), useNoteExtraction()

Feature 3 — AI Chat Interface:
  <LLMChatPanel mode="drawer|side|fullscreen" chapterId? />
    - Markdown rendering (react-markdown + rehype-highlight for code/formulas)
    - LaTeX math rendering (KaTeX for formulas: E = mc²)
    - Streaming responses (token-by-token appearance)
    - Smart suggestions based on current chapter
    - Message history per chapter (persistent in Dexie, synced to Supabase)
    - Provider + model indicator ("Answering with Claude Haiku")
    - Token usage counter (for own-key users)
    - Copy message button
    - "Save as note" button on AI responses
    - Error states: offline, rate limited, invalid key
    Hooks: useLLMChat(), useChatHistory(), useStreamingResponse()

Feature 4 — Study Roadmap:
  <RoadmapView userId />
    - Horizontal scrolling weeks (snap to current week on load)
    - Week card with: theme banner, subject-colored chapter pills, day breakdown
    - Current week highlighted
    - Completion checkmarks on past week items
    - "Regenerate" button (shows diff: what changed from previous plan)
    - Urgency banner (< 6 weeks: red; 6-12: amber; > 12: green)
    - Export to PDF / WhatsApp image
    <RoadmapGenerator /> loading state (shows AI "thinking" steps):
      "Analyzing your progress... 
       Checking 14 incomplete Tier 1 chapters... 
       Building optimal schedule for 47 days remaining...
       Done! Here's your personalized plan 🎯"
    Hooks: useRoadmap(), useRoadmapGeneration()

Feature 5 — Mock Quiz + PYQ:
  <ChapterQuiz chapterId mode="practice|exam" />
    - Question cards with A/B/C/D options (clear tap targets ≥ 48px)
    - Timer per question (90 seconds, animated progress bar)
    - Immediate feedback in practice mode (reveal correct + explanation)
    - No feedback in exam mode (review at end)
    - End screen: score, time taken, question-by-question review
    - "Add to error log" for wrong answers
    - Progress saved to quiz_sessions table
    - Spaced repetition: wrong answers scheduled for 3-day review
    <PYQBrowser /> — filter by year, subject, chapter; question cards
    Hooks: useQuizSession(), useQuestionBank(), useSpacedRepetition()

