## ╔══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╗
## ║  PROMPT 11 — SKILL FILES (FOR AI CODING ASSISTANTS)     ║
## ╚══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╝

Generate all SKILL.md files that AI coding assistants should read
before generating code for StudyOS.

SKILL_FRONTEND.md:
  Section 1: Project Structure (Next.js App Router canonical)
    src/
      app/           — Next.js App Router (route groups: (marketing), (auth), (app))
      components/
        ui/          — shadcn/ui primitives (never modify directly)
        app/         — StudyOS-specific components
      features/      — vertical slices (auth, dashboard, syllabus, notes, chat, quiz)
      shared/        — cross-cutting: hooks, lib, config, types, constants
      server/        — server-only: Supabase clients, auth utils
      db/            — Dexie schema (offline IndexedDB)

  Section 2: Component patterns
    - Always use compound component pattern for complex components
    - Always export both named and default exports
    - Always put prop types as interface above component
    - Prefer React Query for server state over useState + useEffect
    - Always use Zustand for global state (not Context for performance)
    - Virtualize lists with > 20 items (react-virtual)

  Section 3: Styling rules
    - Mobile-first: default styles = mobile; use sm: md: lg: for larger
    - Never use arbitrary Tailwind values ([500px]) — use design tokens
    - Dark mode: use dark: prefix, not separate stylesheets
    - Subject-specific colors: always use physics-*, chemistry-*, biology-* tokens
    - Loading: always skeleton > spinner hierarchy

  Section 4: Performance rules
    - Lazy load routes (React.lazy + Suspense)
    - Memoize expensive computations (useMemo), stable callbacks (useCallback)
    - Images: always use next/image or lazy loading attribute
    - Bundle size: check with vite-bundle-visualizer before PR

SKILL_BACKEND.md:
  Section 1: Supabase Edge Function patterns
    - Always validate JWT at start of every function
    - Always use Zod to validate request body
    - Standard response format: { data, error, meta }
    - Standard error codes with HTTP status mapping
    - Always use transactions for multi-table writes

  Section 2: Database patterns
    - Use views for commonly joined queries
    - Use materialized views for expensive aggregations (daily_stats)
    - Always add updated_at trigger (moddatetime extension)
    - RLS: default deny, explicit allow — test every policy
    - Use pg_cron for scheduled tasks (streak calculation, daily stats rollup)

  Section 3: Realtime patterns
    - Only subscribe to tables that genuinely need real-time (progress, notifications)
    - Always unsubscribe on component unmount
    - Filter subscriptions by user_id to minimize payload

SKILL_AGENTS.md: (see Prompt 4)
SKILL_ANALYTICS.md: (see Prompt 5)
SKILL_SECURITY.md: (see Prompt 9)
SKILL_DESIGN.md: (see Prompt 3)

SKILL_NEET_DOMAIN.md (NEW — critical for AI assistants):
  Purpose: Domain knowledge about NEET that AI must know before generating
  any study-related content or features.
  
  Sections:
    - NEET exam structure (subjects, question counts, marks, negative marking)
    - Chapter tier definitions (Tier 1 = 5+ questions historically)
    - Deleted topics list (never include in study materials or quizzes)
    - Subject weightage (Biology 50%, Physics 25%, Chemistry 25%)
    - Study strategy principles (NCERT-first, diagrams, previous year papers)
    - Common student misconceptions per chapter (so AI avoids reinforcing them)
    - Indian student context (coaching institutes, state boards, dropper year)
    - Sensitive topics (exam stress, pressure — handle with care, never dismissive)

Output: All 8 SKILL.md files in docs/product/skills-app/
  ✅ SKILL_AGENTS.md
  ✅ SKILL_ANALYTICS.md
  ✅ SKILL_BACKEND.md
  ✅ SKILL_DATABASE.md (NEW — migrations + RLS patterns)
  ✅ SKILL_DESIGN.md
  ✅ SKILL_FRONTEND.md
  ✅ SKILL_NEET_DOMAIN.md
  ✅ SKILL_SECURITY.md

