## ║  PROMPT 12 — ADDITIONAL NEET-SPECIFIC FEATURES          ║
## ╚══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╝

Build these additional NEET-specific features that make StudyOS unique.

Feature A — Formula & Reaction Cheatsheet Generator:
  <FormulaSheetGenerator userId />
  - AI scans all completed chapters → extracts formulas, reactions, diagrams
  - Generates one-page formula sheet per subject (Physics / Chemistry)
  - Biology: key diagrams list (Z-scheme, nephron, cardiac cycle)
  - PDF export (A4 landscape, printable)
  - Updates as student completes more chapters
  - Include: formula name, formula itself, units, when to apply

Feature B — Mistake Tracker (Error Log):
  <MistakeTracker userId />
  - When quiz answer is wrong → auto-added to mistake log
  - Student can add manual mistakes ("Always forget lac operon details")
  - AI analyzes patterns: "You make mistakes about: Markovnikov's rule (4x), Bohr model energy levels (3x)"
  - Pre-exam review mode: show all logged mistakes one-by-one
  - Resolve mistakes: "I've understood this now" → moves to resolved

Feature C — NEET Rank Predictor:
  <RankPredictor userId />
  Based on:
    - Chapter completion % (each chapter weighted by NEET weightage)
    - Quiz accuracy per chapter
    - Time to exam
    - Historical NEET score distributions
  Shows:
    - Predicted score range (e.g., "580–620")
    - Estimated All India Rank range
    - Category-wise rank (General/OBC/SC/ST — student selects category)
    - College prediction: "Based on this rank, you may qualify for:"
      - Government Medical Colleges list (state-wise + All India)
    - Disclaimer: "This is an estimate — actual results depend on exam difficulty"
  Data needed: last 5 years NEET score vs rank data (include this as static JSON)

Feature D — Cut-off Tracker:
  <NEETCutoffTracker />
  - Historical NEET cut-offs (2019–2025): All India, State-wise, Category-wise
  - AIIMS, JIPMER, AFMC special cut-offs
  - State-specific counseling quirks (Tamil Nadu NEET merit vs state board)
  - "What score do I need for [college]?" reverse lookup

Feature E — 30-Day Revision Sprint:
  <RevisionSprintPlanner userId />
  - If exam is 30 days away: switch to "Sprint Mode"
  - AI generates compressed revision plan (all 79 chapters in 30 days)
  - 3 chapters per day minimum; high-yield topics first
  - Daily "Rapid Fire" quiz: 20 Qs, 10 mins, all from that day's chapters
  - "Revision not fresh study" — mode focuses on recall not new learning

Feature F — Peer Study Groups (Anonymous):
  <StudyGroupBrowser />
  - Auto-match students studying the same chapter today (anonymous)
  - Shared "chapter challenge": first 5 to complete all subtopics wins
  - Anonymous leaderboard: "325 students completed Current Electricity today"
  - No personal info shown — only study stats

Feature G — Voice Notes (v2):
  <VoiceNoteRecorder />
  - Record audio → Whisper API transcription → OCR-equivalent text pipeline
  - "Explain the Z-scheme to yourself out loud" → AI evaluates answer
  - Helps students who learn by speaking (common Indian learning style)

Output:
  - All feature components
  - Supporting hooks and services
  - NEET static data files (cut-offs, score distributions, college lists)
